  "problem_statement": "fix(providers): detect tunneled Ollama profiles; cap local-model steps\n\n_looks_like_local_ollama() only matched kind==\"ollama\" or \":11434\" in\nthe base_url, so Ollama reverse-proxied behind a custom domain\n(Cloudflare Tunnel, ngrok, ...) was invisible to it despite being the\nsame server. That silently disabled structured/grammar-enforced\ntool-call JSON and the final_answer stop signal for those profiles,\nleaving a small model with no reliable way to signal it was done —\nobserved live as 25+ near-duplicate write_file calls oscillating\ncosmetic diffs for 24 minutes until an unrelated gateway timeout\nkilled the run. Added an explicit LOCAL_OLLAMA_<name> opt-in.\n\nAlso added LOCAL_MODEL_MAX_STEPS (default 15), applied when no\nexplicit step cap is set and the profile looks like local Ollama, so\na stuck small model fails fast instead of running unbounded.\n\nAdded tests/conftest.py: config.py loads the real .env at import\ntime, so ACTIVE_PROFILE (and therefore which code paths default-\nprofile tests exercise) depends on whatever MODEL_PROFILE happens to\nbe set locally. Pins it to \"zai\" for the suite so tests stay isolated\nfrom the developer's live provider config.",
